"money": 0.61}, "rating_margin": 12.5, "sigma_race": 6.5, "sigma_total": 7.14, "baseline_margin": 12.06, "analyst_adjustment": -0.56, "key_factors": ["Democratic-favorable national environment atop a D+3 district", "Matt Little's roughly 2-to-1 fundraising edge and outside backing over Eric Pratt", "Open seat with Angie Craig off the ballot and both nominees new to this electorate", "Markets price a Democratic win near 95 percent; raters split between Likely and Safe D"], "rationale": "Fundamentals point to a double-digit Democratic margin in an open D+3 seat during a favorable environment, and Little has far out-raised Pratt, but thin and partisan-sponsored polling plus market pricing near 95 percent keep this at the top of Likely D rather than Safe.", "watch": "A late shift in the national environment toward Republicans, or Pratt consolidating swing voters after the October debates, could narrow the margin.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Angie Craig (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Minnesota's 2nd District is an open seat after Angie Craig left the House to run for Senate. The district leans Democratic by about three points, and the 2026 national environment favors Democrats, putting the fundamentals well in the party's column. Matt Little enters the general election with a large fundraising advantage over Eric Pratt, having raised roughly twice as much, and outside groups have spent in support of him. Independent ratings mostly place the race in the Likely or Safe Democratic column, and prediction markets price a Democratic win at about 94 to 95 percent.\n\nPolling is limited: a September survey sponsored by Democratic allies showed Little up twelve, while a Republican-sponsored June poll had a narrower five-point margin. Little won a contested primary in August and has campaigned actively, with several debates in October. Given the district's modest Democratic lean, the size of the final margin depends heavily on how the national environment breaks in November.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9565, "margin": 11.37}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9477, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9516, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9571, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9414, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9494, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9241, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9593, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9458, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9592, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9518, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9567, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9516, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9073, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.928, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9436, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9528, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9193, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9436, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.9046, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.9298, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.9495, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.9481, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-15", "p_dem": 0.867, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-16", "p_dem": 0.9332, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-17", "p_dem": 0.9406, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-18", "p_dem": 0.9442, "margin": 11.5}]}